The test calls `dsolve_system` on a system whose second equation has a squared derivative. In `dsolve_system`, the equations are canonicalized and then solved first with `_strong_component_solver`; if that returns no solution, the code falls back to `_component_solver`, which invokes `_weak_component_solver`. In `_weak_component_solver`, if solving the whole component fails and then an individual strongly connected component still gives `scc_sol is None`, the function explicitly raises `NotImplementedError(filldedent(...))` with the message shown there.

## Answer
{"exception_message":"\nThe system of ODEs passed cannot be solved by dsolve_system.","exception_type":"NotImplementedError"}
